From 4d9cdc41f76c820e85e32ae397c6b6aecd9dd10d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:09:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] configs: evb-rk3588: rockusb PID 0x350b -> 0x300a for
 RKDevTool
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 0x350b Kconfig default is the RK3588 BROM maskrom PID — RKDevTool
identifies devices by VID/PID, so our rockusb gadget gets labeled
"MASKROM设备" even while it happily serves the flash protocol. The
vendor usbplug that RKDevTool calls a LOADER device enumerates as
2207:300a (device descriptor verified in out/MiniLoaderAll.bin at
0x26846, followed by the RockChip manufacturer string). Adopt it.
---
 configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig b/configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig
index f4b025057df..4fdc12584a6 100644
--- a/configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig
+++ b/configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig
@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@ CONFIG_USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD=y
 CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ROCKUSB=y
 CONFIG_CMD_ROCKUSB=y
 CONFIG_CMD_USB_MASS_STORAGE=y
+# Rockusb PID: the 0x350b Kconfig default is the RK3588 BROM maskrom PID, so
+# RKDevTool labels our gadget "MASKROM设备". The vendor usbplug — what RKDevTool
+# calls a LOADER device — enumerates as 2207:300a (device descriptor verified
+# in out/MiniLoaderAll.bin @0x26846, "RockChip" string right after). Use that.
+CONFIG_USB_GADGET_PRODUCT_NUM=0x300a
 # vol-up Loader entry: rockchip_dnl_key_pressed() samples the SARADC key
 # ladder at boot; a held vol-up then starts rockusb. The board's other
 # download entry (the maskrom switch) is a BROM-level strap no firmware
-- 
